<p>His full name is Josimar José Évora Dias. He grew up in Mindelo on the island of São Vicente, raised by his grandparents after his father was called to military service and his mother had to work. His grandparents gave him the nickname Vozinha, which roughly translates as “little voice,” and it is now being heard around the world.</p>
<p>He plays for GD Chaves in Liga Portugal 2 — not La Liga, not the Premier League, not the Bundesliga. He has spent his career in Cape Verde, Angola, Moldova, Portugal, Cyprus, and Slovakia. He has never played at a club most football fans could name. On June 15, 2026, at Atlanta Stadium, he became arguably the most discussed goalkeeper on earth.</p>
